IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa27-definitions`

-- coa27-ch5-third-country.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 Chapter 5 "Registered third country
-- auditors" (ss 1241 to 1247), lines 17599-17647 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively); part agent coa27.
--
-- WHAT IS HERE. The two definitions of s 1241, the duties of a registered third country auditor (ss 1242 to 1244),
-- the court's power to order compliance (s 1245) and the reading rule in s 1246(3). Section 1246(1)-(2), (4) (power to
-- make regulations) and s 1247 (an amendment of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act
-- 2004) are machinery, inert in the coverage table.
--
-- READING A RESULT (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE the text says yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own
-- words ("means", "if", "unless", "are not to apply"); NOTHING the text does not decide (silent, limited by its own
-- wording, points outside the text). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Every name begins with its section label.
-- The Secretary of State's functions are exercised as the text says (s 1252 lets a delegation order move them to a body
-- designated by order; that is machinery and is not modelled).

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1241 Meaning of "registered third country auditor" and "UK-traded third country company"
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17604 | “registered third country auditor” means a third country auditor who is entered in the register kept in accordance with regulations under section 1239(1).
@ref s 1241(1) registered third country auditor (src:17604-17604)
GIVEN `the person is a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entered in the register kept in accordance with regulations under section 1239(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1241(1) the person is a registered third country auditor` MEANS
    IF `the person is a third country auditor` AND `the person is entered in the register kept in accordance with regulations under section 1239(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registered third country auditor” means a third country auditor who is entered in the register"

-- src:17605 | (2) In this Part “UK-traded third country company” means a body corporate—
-- src:17606 | (a) which is incorporated or formed under the law of a third country ,
-- src:17607 | (b) whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market ..., and
-- src:17608 | (c) which has not been excluded, or is not of a description of bodies corporate which has been excluded, from this definition by an order made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1241(2) UK-traded third country company (src:17605-17608)
GIVEN `the body corporate is incorporated or formed under the law of a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate has transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate, or a description of bodies corporate to which it belongs, has been excluded by an order made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1241(2) the body corporate is a UK-traded third country company` MEANS
    IF       `the body corporate is incorporated or formed under the law of a third country`
         AND `the body corporate has transferable securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
         AND (NOT `the body corporate, or a description of bodies corporate to which it belongs, has been excluded by an order made by the Secretary of State`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part “UK-traded third country company” means a body corporate"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1242 Duties of registered third country auditors
-- =========================================================================================================

-- Subsection (4): the three kinds of written direction by which the Secretary of State may disapply subsections (1) to (3).
DECLARE `s 1242(4) kind of direction` IS ONE OF
    `s 1242(4)(a) a direction about a particular registered third country auditor or class of them`
    `s 1242(4)(b) a direction about audits of the accounts of a particular UK-traded third country company or class of them`
    `s 1242(4)(c) a direction about audits by a particular registered third country auditor or class of them of the accounts of a particular company or class of them`

-- src:17620 | (4) The Secretary of State may direct in writing that subsections (1) to (3) are not to apply, in whole or in part, in relation to
-- src:17621 | (a) a particular registered third country auditor or class of registered third country auditors.
-- src:17622 | (b) audits of the accounts of a particular UK-traded third country company or class of UK-traded third country companies;
-- src:17623 | (c) audits by a particular registered third country auditor or class of registered third country auditors of the accounts of a particular UK-traded third country company or class of UK-traded third country companies.
@ref s 1242(4) Duties of registered third country auditors: directions disapplying (src:17620-17623)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1242(4) kind of direction`
      `the auditor is within the direction (as a particular auditor or a member of the class)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is within the direction (as a particular company or a member of the class)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1242(4) the direction fits the audit` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1242(4)(a) a direction about a particular registered third country auditor or class of them` THEN
        `the auditor is within the direction (as a particular auditor or a member of the class)`
    WHEN `s 1242(4)(b) a direction about audits of the accounts of a particular UK-traded third country company or class of them` THEN
        `the company is within the direction (as a particular company or a member of the class)`
    WHEN `s 1242(4)(c) a direction about audits by a particular registered third country auditor or class of them of the accounts of a particular company or class of them` THEN
            `the auditor is within the direction (as a particular auditor or a member of the class)`
        AND `the company is within the direction (as a particular company or a member of the class)`

@ref s 1242(4) Duties of registered third country auditors: directions disapplying (src:17620-17623)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has directed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 1242(4) kind of direction`
      `the auditor is within the direction (as a particular auditor or a member of the class)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is within the direction (as a particular company or a member of the class)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction applies to the subsection in question, in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1242(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the audit` MEANS
    IF       `the Secretary of State has directed in writing`
         AND `the direction applies to the subsection in question, in whole or in part`
         AND `s 1242(4) the direction fits the audit` kind `the auditor is within the direction (as a particular auditor or a member of the class)` `the company is within the direction (as a particular company or a member of the class)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsections (1) to (3) are not to apply, in whole or in part"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a direction must be in writing and must fit the auditor, company or audit it names

-- src:17613 | (1) A registered third country auditor who audits the accounts of a UK-traded third country company must participate in—
-- src:17614 | (a) arrangements within paragraph 1 of Schedule 12 (arrangements for independent monitoring of audits . . . ), and
-- src:17615 | (b) arrangements within paragraph 2 of that Schedule (arrangements for independent investigation for disciplinary purposes ...).
@ref s 1242(1) Duties of registered third country auditors: participation (src:17613-17615)
GIVEN `the person is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person audits the accounts of a UK-traded third country company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under subsection (4) disapplies subsection (1) for this audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1242(1) the registered third country auditor must participate in the Schedule 12 arrangements` MEANS
    IF `a direction under subsection (4) disapplies subsection (1) for this audit`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsections (1) to (3) are not to apply" (subsection (4))
    ELSE IF `the person is a registered third country auditor` AND `the person audits the accounts of a UK-traded third country company`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- must participate in the arrangements within paragraph 1 and within paragraph 2 of Schedule 12
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A registered third country auditor who audits the accounts of a UK-traded third country company"

-- src:17616 | (2) A registered third country auditor must—
-- src:17617 | (a) take such steps as may be reasonably required of it to enable its performance of audits of accounts of UK-traded third country companies to be monitored by means of inspections carried out under the arrangements mentioned in subsection (1)(a), and
@ref s 1242(2)(a) Duties of registered third country auditors: steps to enable monitoring (src:17616-17617)
GIVEN `the person is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step is reasonably required of it to enable its performance of audits of the accounts of UK-traded third country companies to be monitored by inspections under the arrangements within paragraph 1 of Schedule 12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under subsection (4) disapplies subsection (2) for this audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1242(2)(a) the registered third country auditor must take the step` MEANS
    IF `a direction under subsection (4) disapplies subsection (2) for this audit`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsections (1) to (3) are not to apply" (subsection (4))
    ELSE IF `the person is a registered third country auditor`
              AND `the step is reasonably required of it to enable its performance of audits of the accounts of UK-traded third country companies to be monitored by inspections under the arrangements within paragraph 1 of Schedule 12`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such steps as may be reasonably required of it"

-- src:17618 | (b) comply with any decision as to disciplinary action to be taken against it made under the arrangements mentioned in subsection (1)(b).
@ref s 1242(2)(b) Duties of registered third country auditors: disciplinary decisions (src:17618-17618)
GIVEN `the person is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a decision as to disciplinary action against it has been made under the arrangements within paragraph 2 of Schedule 12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under subsection (4) disapplies subsection (2) for this audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1242(2)(b) the registered third country auditor must comply with the decision` MEANS
    IF `a direction under subsection (4) disapplies subsection (2) for this audit`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsections (1) to (3) are not to apply" (subsection (4))
    ELSE IF `the person is a registered third country auditor`
              AND `a decision as to disciplinary action against it has been made under the arrangements within paragraph 2 of Schedule 12`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any decision as to disciplinary action to be taken against it made under the arrangements"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1243 Matters to be notified to the Secretary of State
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17626 | (1) The Secretary of State may require a registered third country auditor—
-- src:17627 | (a) to notify him immediately of the occurrence of such events as he may specify in writing and to give him such information in respect of those events as is so specified;
-- src:17628 | (b) to give him, at such times or in respect of such periods as he may specify in writing, such information as is so specified.
-- src:17629 | (2) The notices and information required to be given must be such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part.
@ref s 1243(1)-(2) Matters to be notified: the requirement (src:17626-17629)
GIVEN `the person is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has specified in writing the events, and the information about them, or the information and the times or periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice or information is such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1243(1) the registered third country auditor must notify or give the information` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a registered third country auditor`
         AND `the Secretary of State has specified in writing the events, and the information about them, or the information and the times or periods`
         AND `the notice or information is such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may require a registered third country auditor ... The notices and information required to be given must be such as the Secretary of State may reasonably require"

-- src:17630 | (3) The Secretary of State may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner.
@ref s 1243(3) Matters to be notified: form and verification (src:17630-17630)
GIVEN `the person is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has specified the form, or the manner of verification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1243(3) the registered third country auditor must give the information in the form or verified in the manner` MEANS
    IF `the person is a registered third country auditor` AND `the Secretary of State has specified the form, or the manner of verification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner"

-- src:17631 | (4) Any notice or information required to be given under this section must be given in writing unless the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner.
@ref s 1243(4) Matters to be notified: in writing (src:17631-17631)
GIVEN `the notice or information is given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice or information is given in that other manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1243(4) the notice or information is given as required` MEANS
    IF `the notice or information is given in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner` AND `the notice or information is given in that other manner`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given in writing unless the Secretary of State specifies or approves some other manner"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1244 The Secretary of State's power to call for information
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17633 | (1) The Secretary of State may by notice in writing require a registered third country auditor to give him such information as he may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part.
@ref s 1244(1) Power to call for information (src:17633-17633)
GIVEN `the person is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has required the information by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is such as he may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1244(1) the registered third country auditor must give the information` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a registered third country auditor`
         AND `the Secretary of State has required the information by notice in writing`
         AND `the information is such as he may reasonably require for the exercise of his functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by notice in writing require a registered third country auditor to give him such information as he may reasonably require"

-- src:17634 | (2) The Secretary of State may require that any information which he requires under this section is to be given within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as he may specify.
@ref s 1244(2) Power to call for information: time (src:17634-17634)
GIVEN `the last day of the reasonable time the Secretary of State specified` IS A DATE
      `the day the information was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1244(2) the information was given within the time specified` MEANS
    IF `the day the information was given` AT MOST `the last day of the reasonable time the Secretary of State specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within such reasonable time ... as he may specify" (a period fixed in the Secretary of State's own specification: the ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1245 Compliance orders
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17637 | (1) If at any time it appears to the Secretary of State that a registered third country auditor has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part, the Secretary of State may make an application to the court under this section.
@ref s 1245(1) Compliance orders: the application (src:17637-17637)
GIVEN `the person is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the auditor has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1245(1) the Secretary of State may apply to the court` MEANS
    IF `the person is a registered third country auditor` AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that the auditor has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If at any time it appears to the Secretary of State that a registered third country auditor has failed to comply ... the Secretary of State may make an application" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q1)

-- src:17638 | (2) If on an application under this section the court decides that the auditor has failed to comply with the obligation in question, it may order the auditor to take such steps as the court directs for securing that the obligation is complied with.
@ref s 1245(2) Compliance orders: the court's order (src:17638-17638)
GIVEN `an application has been made to the court under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decides that the auditor has failed to comply with the obligation in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1245(2) the court may order the auditor to take steps` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made to the court under this section` AND `the court decides that the auditor has failed to comply with the obligation in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- it may order the auditor to take such steps as the court directs for securing that the obligation is complied with
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under this section the court decides that the auditor has failed to comply with the obligation in question, it may order" (an "on an application ... the court decides" gate: the where/when kind, listed and not flipped in the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12)

DECLARE `s 1245(3) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 1245(3) the High Court`
    `s 1245(3) the Court of Session`

-- src:17639 | (3) In this section “the court” means the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
@ref s 1245(3) Compliance orders: "the court" (src:17639-17639)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1245(3) court`
`s 1245(3) the court is` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in Scotland` THEN `s 1245(3) the Court of Session` ELSE `s 1245(3) the High Court`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1246 Removal of third country auditors from the register of auditors
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1246(3) person keeping the register` IS ONE OF
    `s 1246(3) the person keeping the register in accordance with regulations under section 1239(1)`
    `s 1246(3) the person keeping the part of the register which relates to third country auditors`

-- src:17643 | (3) Where provision is made under section 1239(4) (different parts of the register to be kept by different persons), references in this section to the person keeping the register are to the person keeping that part of the register which relates to third country auditors.
@ref s 1246(3) Removal of third country auditors: the person keeping the register (src:17643-17643)
GIVEN `provision is made under section 1239(4) for different parts of the register to be kept by different persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1246(3) person keeping the register`
`s 1246(3) the references in this section to the person keeping the register are to` MEANS
    IF `provision is made under section 1239(4) for different parts of the register to be kept by different persons`
    THEN `s 1246(3) the person keeping the part of the register which relates to third country auditors`
    ELSE `s 1246(3) the person keeping the register in accordance with regulations under section 1239(1)`
